  "id": "funnel_oep_overdispersion",
  "reference": "Spiegelhalter DJ, Quality & Safety in Health Care 2005;14:347-351 \u2014 O/E funnel with the winsorized multiplicative over-dispersion adjustment. Twelve providers whose O/E ratios vary far more than Poisson allows: phi-hat = 6.228815, so limits widen by sqrt(phi) = 2.4958. The same data on chart='oe' flags 3 of 12 providers at 99.8%, which is not credible as a rate of genuine outliers; the adjusted chart flags none, having recognised the spread as unmodelled between-provider variation rather than exceptional performance. Residuals use the variance-stabilising transform z = 2*(sqrt(O) - sqrt(cl*E)) and are winsorized at the 10th/90th percentiles before squaring.",
